KNOWN ISSUES / TECHNICAL DEBT
=============================

Dream Spawn Damage
------------------

Dream spawn currently uses a fixed X/Z region and searches vertically
for terrain.

If the terrain around that location is destroyed or heavily modified
(for example by exploding beds), a later Dream entry may find an unsafe
surface or allow the player to fall into the void.

Possible future solutions:

- Search outward for a valid safe spawn location
- Protect the Dream entrance area
- Regenerate the entrance area when needed
- Spawn into a generated entrance room
- Replace this system entirely when procedural Dream generation exists


Player Death
------------

Player death while Dreaming may leave the DreamSession active.

Future work must define:

- whether death immediately wakes the player
- where the player respawns
- whether Dream inventory/progression is lost
- when the persistent session is cleared


Return Position
---------------

Current bed-triggered wake behavior works correctly using BlockPos.

Possible future improvement if required:

- vanilla-style safe bed wake location
- exact X/Y/Z for debug-command entry
- yaw/pitch restoration
- behavior when the original bed has been destroyed


Dream Duration
--------------

Dream duration is still hardcoded.

Future:
- configuration
- gameplay-dependent duration
- progression-dependent duration


Offline Timer Semantics
-----------------------

Current behavior:
    Dream timer pauses while offline.

Future option:
    Store an absolute world/server game-time deadline so Dream time
    can continue progressing while offline.



